{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        The rooms directory is the reference guide to the building: every room,
        organised by floor, with its room type, bed size, bathroom style, view,
        and any tags or comments staff have added.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the directory</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>Open <strong>Directory → Rooms Directory</strong> and pick a floor.</li>
        <li>Select a room to see its details and comments.</li>
        <li>
            Add a comment when you learn something the next person should know:
            a quirk with the heating, a guest preference, a maintenance note.
        </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>For managers</h2>
    <p>
        With rooms manage permission, two extra menu items appear:
        <strong>Manage Floors</strong>, where floors and their features are laid
        out, and <strong>Room Types</strong>, where the shared definitions
        (bed size, bathroom, view) that rooms reference are maintained. Set up
        room types first, since every room needs one.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
